{"name":"Botanist","hex":"#9ad28c","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"botanist","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A person engaged in botany, the scientific study of plants."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/botanist"}],"entries":[{"title":"Botanist (band)","blocks":[{"text":"Botanist is an American black metal band based in San Francisco, originally formed as a one-man project by musician Otrebor, with later collaborations with other musicians. The band has been described as a \"Guitarless, environmentally themed 'green metal' project utilizing hammered dulcimer, sung from the perspective of a reclusive, nature-loving misanthrope.\" Most of the band's lyrics are based on environmental themes and botanical processes, with a focus on climate change and destruction of the natural world."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Botanist_(band)","wikidata":"Q16247407"},{"title":"Botany","blocks":[{"text":"Botany, also called plant science, is the branch of natural science and biology that studies the growth, reproduction and evolution of plants over the last 3.5 billion years of life on earth. As with all areas of biology and medicine, plants can be studied at range of levels from their biochemistry, molecular biology, cell biology and genetics to their ecology, pathology, anatomy, morphology and taxonomy. A botanist or plant scientist is a scientist who specialises in this field. Plants can be defined in multiple ways including approximately 410,000 species of land plants, and some 391,000 species of vascular plants, of which approximately 369,000 are flowering plants and approximately 20,000 bryophytes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6c/Myris_fragr_Fr_080112-3294_ltn.jpg/330px-Myris_fragr_Fr_080112-3294_ltn.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Botany","wikidata":"Q441"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Cork_Micrographia_Hooke.png/500px-Cork_Micrographia_Hooke.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/17/Cork_Micrographia_Hooke.png/500px-Cork_Micrographia_Hooke.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"An engraving of the cells of cork, from Robert Hooke's Micrographia, 1665","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ACork_Micrographia_Hooke.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Renaissance_C14_F%C3%BCllmaurer_Leonhart_Fuchs.jpg/500px-Renaissance_C14_F%C3%BCllmaurer_Leonhart_Fuchs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Renaissance_C14_F%C3%BCllmaurer_Leonhart_Fuchs.jpg/1280px-Renaissance_C14_F%C3%BCllmaurer_Leonhart_Fuchs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/40/Renaissance_C14_F%C3%BCllmaurer_Leonhart_Fuchs.jpg/500px-Renaissance_C14_F%C3%BCllmaurer_Leonhart_Fuchs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARenaissance_C14_F%C3%BCllmaurer_Leonhart_Fuchs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Brunfels-1.png/500px-Brunfels-1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/68/Brunfels-1.png/500px-Brunfels-1.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABrunfels-1.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/6a/Hieronymus_Bock_%281546%29.jpg/500px-Hieronymus_Bock_%281546%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src